---
// Evidence-led guide separates GeM's available signing methods from bid-specific requirements.
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleEndNote from "@/components/ArticleEndNote.astro";
import { dscGuideFaqs } from "@/data/dsc";
import "@/styles/services.css";

const title = "Is DSC Mandatory for GeM? eSign vs DSC Explained";
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "Guides", path: "/guides/" },
  { name: "Is DSC mandatory for GeM?", path: "/guides/is-dsc-mandatory-for-gem/" }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description="Is DSC compulsory for GeM registration or bidding? See when GeM permits OTP or eSign, when a bid may require DSC, and what to check first."
  article={{ headline: title, publishDate: "2026-09-29", updatedDate: "2026-09-29", section: "GeM service guides" }}
  faqs={dscGuideFaqs}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="service-page">
    <header class="service-intro"><div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/guides/">Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>GeM eSign and DSC</span></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Service guide / Government e-Marketplace</p>
      <h1>Is DSC mandatory for GeM? Check the transaction and the bid.</h1>
      <p class="intro-copy"><strong>Do not assume every GeM seller needs a DSC.</strong> GeM's published material says documents and transactions can be verified using OTP, eSign or a Digital Signature Certificate. A particular bid or portal step may still require a valid DSC.</p>
      <p class="fine">By Porul.in · Published and reviewed <time datetime="2026-09-29">29 September 2026</time> · Commercial service guide</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button button--dark" href="#decision-checklist">Check your situation →</a><a href="/digital-signature-for-gem/">Get help obtaining a GeM DSC</a></div>
    </div></header>

    <section class="service-band"><div class="wrap service-split">
      <div><h2>For seller registration</h2><p>Do not purchase a DSC solely because you are opening a GeM seller account. Use the verification option shown in the current registration and profile workflow. GeM's official eSign and DSC material describes eSign verification for both buyers and sellers.</p><p>If the portal gives you a specific DSC instruction, save the exact message before asking for help.</p></div>
      <div><h2>For bid participation</h2><p>Read the bid document, additional terms and the live submission step. Some bid instructions expressly require bidders to use a valid DSC. Other GeM transactions may offer OTP or eSign. The requirement attached to the actual transaction is more reliable than a universal internet checklist.</p><p>Leave time to complete certificate verification and system setup before the closing date.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="service-band" aria-labelledby="difference-title"><div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="difference-title">eSign and DSC are different signing routes</h2>
      <div class="service-grid">
        <article><h3>OTP</h3><p>GeM's published FAQ lists OTP as one way a document or transaction may be verified. Availability depends on the portal step.</p></article>
        <article><h3>eSign</h3><p>GeM describes an online eSign verification process available to buyers and sellers. Follow the identity and consent steps shown in the current portal.</p></article>
        <article><h3>DSC</h3><p>A Digital Signature Certificate uses certificate-based signing, commonly through a USB token. The certificate must belong to the appropriate signer and remain valid for the required transaction.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">These descriptions explain the available routes; they do not establish which route GeM will present for every account, bid or transaction.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="service-band" id="decision-checklist"><div class="wrap service-split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Decision checklist</p><h2>Check these five things before buying a DSC.</h2><p>This avoids paying for the wrong applicant, certificate configuration or validity while a bid deadline is approaching.</p></div>
      <ol class="service-steps">
        <li><strong>Identify the exact task.</strong> Is this seller registration, profile verification, catalogue work, contract signing or bid submission?</li>
        <li><strong>Read the live instruction.</strong> Save the portal message and search the bid document and additional terms for signing requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Identify the signer.</strong> Confirm which authorised person is responsible for the business declaration or bid.</li>
        <li><strong>Check what already exists.</strong> Record any current certificate's holder, type and expiry date, without sharing its PIN.</li>
        <li><strong>Work backward from the deadline.</strong> Allow for KYC, certificate issuance, token delivery or setup and a test before final submission.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="service-band"><div class="wrap service-split">
      <div><h2>If the bid requires a DSC</h2><p>Confirm the authorised signatory, requested certificate type, validity, USB token and system requirements before ordering. The Controller of Certifying Authorities advises applicants to obtain certificates through licensed certifying authorities.</p><p>Porul offers <a href="/digital-signature-for-gem/">Class 3 DSC and USB-token support for GeM users</a> through PantaSign and emSigner partner channels. The written quote identifies the provider route, certificate details, fee and support included.</p></div>
      <div><h2>If eSign is available</h2><p>Follow the current GeM workflow rather than purchasing a DSC only because a third-party article calls it universally mandatory. Make sure the authorised person controls the relevant identity and contact method and understands the declaration being signed.</p><p>If eSign fails, preserve the exact error and use GeM's current support route before changing account information repeatedly.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="service-band" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions about DSC and GeM bidding</h2>
      {dscGuideFaqs.map(({ question, answer }) => <details><summary>{question}</summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}
    </div></section>

    <section class="service-band" aria-labelledby="sources-title"><div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="sources-title">Official sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://assets-bg.gem.gov.in/resources/upload/shared_doc/training_content/E-Sign-DSC-Process-1685708713.pdf">GeM eSign and DSC process workflow</a> — the official training document describing verification routes and the eSign process for buyers and sellers.</li>
        <li><a href="https://gem.gov.in/userFaqs/seller">GeM seller FAQs</a> — states that documents and transactions can be verified using OTP, eSign or digital signature.</li>
        <li><a href="https://assets-bg.gem.gov.in/resources/upload/shared_doc/gtc/GeM-GTC-40-1740735825.pdf">GeM General Terms and Conditions, version 1.22</a> — official terms that describe eSign at par with digital signatures.</li>
        <li><a href="https://cca.gov.in/digital_signature.html">Controller of Certifying Authorities: how to obtain a DSC</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fine">Official material was reviewed on 29 September 2026. Always check the current GeM screen, bid document, corrigenda and additional conditions for the transaction you intend to complete.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="service-band"><div class="wrap">
      <h2>Need a certificate after checking the requirement?</h2>
      <p>Porul.in provides independent paid DSC assistance for GeM users in Tamil Nadu. Share the transaction or bid, the authorised-signatory role, any existing certificate and the deadline. Do not send identity documents, passwords, OTPs or DSC PINs in the initial enquiry.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button button--dark" href="/enquire/?service=dsc">Prepare a GeM DSC enquiry →</a><a href="/digital-signature-for-gem/">Review the DSC service scope</a><a href="/guides/gem-seller-registration/">Read the seller registration guide</a></div>
      <p class="fine">This guide supports Porul's DSC service and is not an independent review of Porul. Porul is not affiliated with GeM or the government. Certificate issuance and portal acceptance are decided by the relevant providers and authorities. For corrections, email <a href="mailto:hello@porul.in?subject=GeM%20DSC%20guide%20correction">hello@porul.in</a>.</p>
    </div></section>
    <ArticleEndNote />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
